# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ustaad.com — .gitignore
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. Nothing below is a convenience rule.
# NFR-4, SEC-25 and §10.2 of the specification all depend on this file:
# no credential, no user data and no database file may ever be committed.
# If you add a new secret-bearing or data-bearing path, add it here in the
# same change that introduces it — never afterwards.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Database files (user data lives outside the repo, always) -------------
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
local.db
local.db-journal

# --- Dependencies and build output -----------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT root-anchored. The backend now lives under Backend/ and the
# client under client/, so a leading-slash rule would match neither. An ignore
# rule that silently stops matching is worse than no rule, because the file it
# was protecting looks protected.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
coverage/

# --- Uploaded / generated user artefacts ------------------------------------
# CNIC images, academic documents and volunteer CVs live in the private
# Supabase Storage bucket. If anything ever lands on local disk, it stops here.
# Unanchored for the same reason as above: this one guards identity documents,
# so it is the last rule that should quietly stop matching.
uploads/
tmp/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# --- Tooling and editor noise ------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.drizzle/
.netlify/
.vercel/
.turbo/
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
